A super fine analog clock displaying system time. It leverages GTK4,
Cairo, and librsvg to produce a time display with pretty-pixels.

Original project by MacSlow (2006). This is a 20th anniversary
GTK4 port by Evan Slower (2026).

There are three improvements which are not original.  
1. A second 'Custom' button has been added.
2. The themes menu is now in alphabetical order.
3. And 31 extra themes have also been added to raise total to 50.

Also important to note, all hotkeys have been removed. And functionality for
'show in taskbar' and 'show in pager' are no longer present.

I chose to use the zen_MacSlow theme as the new default theme.  Mirco "MacSlow"
Müller has had 20 more years to zen out as we all have. It's fitting I think. 
Here is the meson.build for the 50 themes names and attributes to the creators.
I love these themes and I hope you'll enjoy them on your desktop the way I do.

